  "lineage": "Kelantanese Malay competitive group-singing form consolidated in the mid-20th century on the Malaysia-Thailand border and popularized nationally from the 1980s, in which a tukang karut improvises rhyming pantun verse and a juara leads while a seated awok-awok chorus of twenty or more answers in unison with synchronized hand-clapping and body movement, driven by rebana and kompang frame drums, canang kettle gongs and a gong, accelerating from a slow declamatory opening to a fast interlocked chant.",
